ui-use-back-to-return-to-the-previous-screen-or-menu-to-open-product-navigation-keep-the-lead = Use Back to return to the previous screen, or Menu to open product navigation. Keep the leading button aligned to the leading edge.

ui-headline = Headline

ui-the-headline-can-describe-the-current-page-the-current-section-or-the-product-headline-tex = The headline can describe the current page, the current section, or the product. Headline text should be brief enough to easily fit in the app bar.

ui-in-medium-flexible-and-large-flexible-app-bars-the-headline-can-wrap-to-a-second-line-don = In medium flexible and large flexible app bars, the headline can wrap to a second line. Don't truncate the headline text, and don't wrap text in a small app bar.

ui-if-headline-text-is-long-use-a-medium-flexible-or-large-flexible-app-bar-and-wrap-the-head = If headline text is long, use a medium flexible or large flexible app bar and wrap the headline to two lines maximum

ui-headlines-can-be-aligned-to-the-leading-edge-or-centered-the-headline-s-typography-style-d = Headlines can be aligned to the leading edge or centered. The headline's typography style depends on the app bar size.

ui-headline-typography-small-uses-title-large-medium-flexible-uses-headline-medium-and-large = Headline typography: small uses title large, medium flexible uses headline medium, and large flexible uses display small

ui-subtitles-are-aligned-with-their-headline-their-typography-style-depends-on-the-app-bar-si = Subtitles are aligned with their headline. Their typography style depends on the app bar size.

ui-subtitle-typography-small-uses-label-medium-medium-flexible-uses-label-large-and-large-fle = Subtitle typography: small uses label medium, medium flexible uses label large, and large flexible uses title medium

ui-trailing-icon-buttons = Trailing icon buttons

ui-trailing-icon-buttons-are-aligned-to-the-trailing-edge-of-the-app-bar-place-most-used-acti = Trailing icon buttons are aligned to the trailing edge of the app bar. Place most-used actions closest to the leading edge.

ui-avoid-using-these-buttons-to-open-a-menu-with-more-actions-if-more-actions-are-needed-plac = Avoid using these buttons to open a menu with more actions. If more actions are needed, place them in a toolbar instead. If changing the icon button color style to filled or tonal, only use one icon button.

ui-use-filled-icons-when-possible-for-the-best-visibility-outlined-icons-can-also-be-used-par = Use filled icons when possible for the best visibility. Outlined icons can also be used, particularly for unselected toggle buttons.

ui-adaptive-design-allows-an-interface-to-respond-or-change-based-on-context-such-as-the-user = Adaptive design allows an interface to respond or change based on context, such as the user, device, and usage.

ui-the-width-of-the-app-bar-container-responds-to-the-view-or-device-width-it-should-always-s = The width of the app bar container responds to the view or device width. It should always span 100% of the window width.

ui-the-app-bar-s-container-responds-to-always-fill-the-window-width = The app bar's container responds to always fill the window width

ui-resizing-app-bar = Resizing app bar

ui-resizing-may-cause-actions-at-the-trailing-edge-of-the-app-bar-to-collapse-into-an-overflo = Resizing may cause actions at the trailing edge of the app bar to collapse into an overflow menu at smaller breakpoints. These actions become visible again at larger sizes.

ui-in-an-expanded-window-every-trailing-action-stays-visible = In an expanded window, every trailing action stays visible

ui-actions-at-the-trailing-edge-collapse-into-an-overflow-menu = Actions at the trailing edge collapse into an overflow menu

ui-the-search-container-of-the-search-app-bar-should-fill-100-of-the-space-between-leading-an = The search container of the search app bar should fill 100% of the space between leading and trailing app bar elements until it reaches 312dp. Then, it should only grow further to fill 50% of that space.

ui-the-search-field-grows-with-the-window-until-it-reaches-312dp-then-grows-at-half-the-rate = The search field grows with the window until it reaches 312dp, then grows at half the rate

ui-the-app-bar-automatically-supports-right-to-left-rtl-languages-by-aligning-the-layout-of-e = The app bar automatically supports right-to-left (RTL) languages by aligning the layout of elements to the leading and trailing edges of the container. This means that in RTL languages, the layout of the app bar is mirrored.

ui-tessera-does-not-provide-a-layout-direction-yet-the-right-to-left-bar-below-is-arranged-by = Tessera does not provide a layout direction yet. The right-to-left bar below is arranged by hand to show the mirrored result; the native app bar always lays out left to right.

ui-left-to-right-navigation-at-the-leading-edge-actions-at-the-trailing-edge = Left-to-right: navigation at the leading edge, actions at the trailing edge

ui-right-to-left-the-layout-is-mirrored-with-navigation-on-the-right-and-actions-on-the-left = Right-to-left: the layout is mirrored, with navigation on the right and actions on the left

ui-app-bars-should-initially-be-the-same-color-as-the-background-then-fill-with-a-contrasting = App bars should initially be the same color as the background, then fill with a contrasting color on scroll to provide visual separation from the background. The app bar can remain on a page at all times, or can hide and reappear when scrolling.

ui-a-flat-app-bar-matches-the-background = A flat app bar matches the background

ui-upon-scrolling-an-app-bar-container-fills-with-contrasting-color-to-create-a-visual-separa = Upon scrolling, an app bar container fills with contrasting color to create a visual separation

ui-to-focus-more-on-body-content-consider-setting-the-app-bar-container-to-be-transparent-on = To focus more on body content, consider setting the app bar container to be transparent on scroll. This allows the buttons to float above the content. Make sure icon buttons have a container fill.

ui-a-transparent-app-bar-lets-filled-icon-buttons-float-above-the-content = A transparent app bar lets filled icon buttons float above the content

ui-when-scrolled-medium-flexible-and-large-flexible-app-bars-can-transform-into-small-app-bar = When scrolled, medium flexible and large flexible app bars can transform into small app bars. They should remain small until the page is scrolled back to the top. Don't transform app bars into a search app bar.

ui-the-app-bar-can-hide-when-scrolling-up-and-reveal-when-scrolling-down = The app bar can hide when scrolling up and reveal when scrolling down

ui-medium-and-large-flexible-app-bars-can-use-the-compress-effect-to-transform-into-small-app = Medium and large flexible app bars can use the compress effect to transform into small app bars when scrolled

