ui-when-hovered-the-hover-state-provides-a-visual-cue-to-the-user-that-the-element-is-interac = When hovered, the hover state provides a visual cue to the user that the element is interactive. When clicked (in both active and inactive states), a ripple appears to indicate feedback.

ui-keyboard-or-switch = Keyboard or switch

ui-when-navigating-to-an-interactive-element-a-focus-indicator-appears-to-show-that-action-ca = When navigating to an interactive element, a focus indicator appears to show that action can be taken. When the element is selected, an action is then performed.

ui-focus-should-initially-land-on-the-leading-button-since-it-s-the-first-interactive-element = Focus should initially land on the leading button, since it's the first interactive element of the app bar. The Tab key navigates from the first button to the second button in the app bar, and Space or Enter activates the focused action.

ui-tab-moves-through-the-app-bar-from-the-leading-button-space-or-enter-activates-the-focused = Tab moves through the app bar from the leading button; Space or Enter activates the focused action

