ui-screen-readers-will-read-the-ui-text-followed-by-the-component-s-role-the-headline-has-the = Screen readers will read the UI text followed by the component's role. The headline has the accessibility role Title; AccessKit has no Title role, so this example exposes the headline as a Heading whose label combines the headline and subtitle.

ui-label-icon-buttons-according-to-their-accessibility-guidelines-the-app-bar-icon-button-has = Label icon buttons according to their accessibility guidelines. The app bar icon button has the accessibility role Button, and should be clearly labeled with the action it takes, like View on map.

ui-an-app-bar-s-accessibility-label-can-incorporate-its-ui-text-as-well-as-additional-context = An app bar's accessibility label can incorporate its UI text as well as additional context, and an icon button is labeled with the action it takes

